<title>UK: UK unemployment falls 36,500 in June.</title>
<headline>UK unemployment falls 36,500 in June.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released the following provisional data for unemployment in June and average earnings in May. (Previous estimates in brackets, minus denotes fall, data seasonally adjusted unless indicated)</p>
<p>   UNEMPLOYMENT			JUNE	MAY     (PREL MAY)</p>
<p>    Monthly change		  -36,500   -17,100   (-18,400)</p>
<p>    Rate (pct)			 5.7	5.8	    (5.8)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj change    -70,400    n/a	(-67,500)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj rate (pct) 5.5	 5.8	    (5.8)</p>
<p>NOTE - Mkts forecast 25,000 June unemployment fall  </p>
<p>    Unemployment level (mln)     1.601*    1.637	(1.636)</p>
<p>    Unemployment level unadj     1.550     1.620	 (1.620)</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 3m adj   -36,700   -36,900   (-37,400)</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 6m	 -47,100   -48,800   (-49,000)</p>
<p>   AVERAGE EARNINGS		  MAY	 APRIL   (PREL APR)</p>
<p>   underlying yearly chng (pct)  4.25	4.5	    (4.5)</p>
<p>   index (base 1990)		 136.4     137.0	(137.1)</p>
<p>   actual yearly chng (pct)	4.2	 4.2	    (4.2)</p>
<p>By sector (annual pct chng)</p>
<p>   Production-- underlying	 4.25	4.25	  (4.25)</p>
<p>		 -- actual	     4.6	 4.0	    (3.9)</p>
<p>    Manufacturing -- underlying  4.25	4.25	  (4.25)</p>
<p>			-- actual	4.4	 4.0	    (3.8)</p>
<p>    Services -- underlying	 4.5	 4.75	  (4.75)</p>
<p>		 -- actual	     3.9	 4.3	    (4.4)</p>
<p>NOTE: consensus forecast 4.5 pct for overall underlying average earnings.</p>
<p>    UNIT WAGE COSTS		  MAY	 APRIL   (PREL APR)</p>
<p>    Monthly change vs yr ago     3.4	 1.4	    (1.6)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)		116.3     114.5	(115.1)</p>
<p>    3-mth versus same yr/ago     2.4	 2.1	    (2.2)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)		115.2     114.6	(115.5)</p>
<p>    PRODUCTIVITY		     MAY	 APRIL   (PREL APR)</p>
<p>    Monthly change vs yr ago     0.9	 2.5	    (2.1)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)		122.7     124.0	(123.1)</p>
<p>    3-mth versus same yr/ago     1.7	 2.1	    (1.9)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)		123.5     123.8	(122.9)</p>
<p>OVERALL EMPLOYMENT (THOUSANDS, S/ADJ)</p>
<p>    EMPLOYEES IN EMPLOYMENT	Q1	  Q4 1996    Q1 1996</p>
<p>    LEVEL				22,459    22,355	22,111</p>
<p>    CHANGE			     104	 51		 -29</p>
<p>WORKFORCE IN EMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>    LEVEL				26,209    26,122	25,849</p>
<p>    CHANGE			     86	  43		 -65</p>
<p>    JOB CENTRE VACANCIES	   JUNE	MAY     (PREL MAY)</p>
<p>    Level				282,400   274,300  (274,300)</p>
<p>    Change			    +8,100**   -300	  (-300)</p>
<p>    Avg 3m change		   +2,400     +900	  (+900)</p>
<p>Lowest rate since August 1990.</p>
<p>* Lowest level since April 1990.</p>
<p>** Highest since 1980, when the series began.</p>
